
{
  "metadata": {
    "description": "HealthBridge AI - US health insurance enrollment, maintenance and renewal assistant"
    "sample_queries": [
      "I want to enroll in a health insurance plan.",
      "I need to update my address on my policy.",
      "I want to renew my health insurance policy."
    ]
  },

  include "config/llm_config.hocon",

  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "HealthcareCoordinator",
      "function": {
        "description": "Coordinates health insurance enrollment, policy maintenance and renewal requests."
      },

"instructions": """
You are HealthcareCoordinator, the main orchestration agent
for HealthBridge AI.

You coordinate three specialist agents:

1. EnrollmentAgent
   Handles new fictional health insurance enrollments.

2. MaintenanceAgent
   Handles fictional insurance policy maintenance.

3. RenewalAgent
   Handles fictional insurance renewals.
   This agent has access to PolicyLookupTool,
   RenewalValidationTool, and RenewalRequestTool.

IMPORTANT DELEGATION RULES:

- When the customer asks about policy renewal,
  invoke RenewalAgent.

- When the customer requests policy lookup or
  renewal eligibility, invoke RenewalAgent.

- RenewalAgent owns the policy lookup and validation
  tools. You do not need to call them directly.

- Do not tell the customer that policy lookup tools
  are unavailable without first delegating to RenewalAgent.

- When the customer requests enrollment,
  invoke EnrollmentAgent.

- When the customer requests policy maintenance,
  invoke MaintenanceAgent.

- Never invent policy records, premiums, or eligibility.

- Do not create a renewal request unless the application
  has verified customer identity and explicit consent.

- For read-only requests, retrieve and validate information
  without creating or modifying records.

- This is a fictional insurance demonstration.
  No real insurance coverage is issued or changed.
""",
      "tools": [
        "EnrollmentAgent",
        "MaintenanceAgent",
        "RenewalAgent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "EnrollmentAgent",
      "function": {
        "description": "Guides customers through new health insurance enrollment."
      },
      "instructions": """
You are the HealthBridge Enrollment Agent.

Explain the fictional enrollment workflow.
Identify missing application information.
Help customers understand simulated plan options.

Do not determine real insurance eligibility or activate coverage.
""",
      "tools": []
    },
    {
      "name": "MaintenanceAgent",
      "function": {
        "description": "Handles requests to update existing insurance policy information."
      },
      "instructions": """
You are the HealthBridge Policy Maintenance Agent.

Help customers prepare requests to update addresses,
contact details and dependent information.

Identify missing information and explain the next steps.
Never claim a policy record was updated without a successful tool result.
""",
      "tools": []
    },
    
{
  "name": "RenewalAgent",
"function": {
  "description": "Retrieve fictional policy information and validate renewal eligibility. Pass the customer's policy ID when invoking this agent.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "policy_id": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Fictional policy ID supplied by the customer, such as HB-1001."
      }
    },
    "required": ["policy_id"]
  }
},
  "instructions": """
You are the HealthBridge Policy Renewal Agent.

You help customers with fictional health insurance policy renewals.

When a customer requests a renewal:
1. Ask for the fictional policy ID if missing.
2. Call PolicyLookupTool to retrieve the policy.
3. Call RenewalValidationTool to check renewal readiness.
4. If validation identifies issues, explain them clearly.
5. If validation passes, explain the next steps and ask
   for customer confirmation.
6. Never claim that renewal is complete without a
   successful authorized transaction result.

Never invent policy information, renewal approval, or premium amounts.
Never claim that a policy was renewed unless an authorized renewal
tool explicitly confirms that action.


After PolicyLookupTool and RenewalValidationTool succeed,
explain the fictional renewal details and ask the customer
to confirm the exact action.

Never call RenewalRequestTool unless the application has
verified an explicit confirmation for this policy and action.
Do not invent or set customer_confirmed to true yourself.

If confirmed and authorized, call RenewalRequestTool.
Report the returned request ID and Pending Review status.

A pending request does not mean coverage has been renewed.
If validation fails, explain the issues without creating a request.


This is a demonstration using fictional insurance records.
""",
    "tools": [
    "PolicyLookupTool",
    "RenewalValidationTool"
  ]
},

{
  "name": "PolicyLookupTool",
  "class": "healthbridge.policy_lookup_tool.PolicyLookupTool",
  "function": {
    "description": "Retrieve a fictional insurance policy by its policy ID from the HealthBridge SQLite database.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "policy_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The fictional insurance policy ID, for example HB-1001."
        }
      },
      "required": ["policy_id"]
    }
  }
},

{
  "name": "RenewalValidationTool",
  "class": "healthbridge.renewal_validation_tool.RenewalValidationTool",
  "function": {
    "description": "Validate a fictional health insurance policy for the demonstration renewal workflow. Check policy status, required information, and a simulated 60-day renewal window.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "policy_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The fictional insurance policy ID, for example HB-1001."
        }
      },
      "required": ["policy_id"]
    }
  }
},


  ]
}
